>
> What can I do to get out of this shop without getting killed?

Here are possibilities of getting out, from least desireable to most:
1) Destroy the door with kicking or striking.
2) Immediately zap the wand of polymorph at yourself.
3) Zap the wand of polymorph at the shopkeeper.
4) Drop your stuff first, then polymorph yourself.
5) Write a scroll of teleport.

Choice one is obviously undesirable, as the shopkeeper will start
fighting you, but since you have magic resistance, you can survive
several hits as he drains his wand on you first. However, he's an
intelligent creature and will follow you up the stairs, so you probably
don't want to do this, especially on an unexplored level.
Choice two isn't that bad, but if you drop your stuff inadventently the
shopkeeper will claim it. Plus, you might turn into something lame,
like you suggested, or you might system-shock yourself to oblivion.
Choice three is actually quite viable; drop all the shop items into a
stack in a corner of the shop (out of the way of magic) first. Even if
the shopkeeper doesn't succumb to the first polymorph bolt, keep
zapping. He'll either a) turn into something lame, at which point you
can just kill him, b) shudder for a moment and die, which is murder but
solves your problem, c) turn into something powerful and kill you, or
d) kill you outright.
Choice four is better than you might think; the odds are good that
you'll turn into something stronger than a level two wizard. Besides,
if you die in your polymorphed form, you can still revert to your
original form. (But that probably won't help you much, as your max HP
is probably quite low already.
Choice five you ruled out all together, but did you know that you can
write on labeled scrolls? True, it abuses wisdom, but that's not such a
bad penalty. Even if you haven't identified scrolls of teleport,
wizards have a 2/3 base chance of getting the scroll right.



